minios-module-manager (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Redesign the interface around native GTK tabs for module management and
    module creation, with separate Running Now and Next Boot views, contextual
    help, header Back navigation, and scrollable creation workflows.
  * Add build-base stack selection to package, script, and interactive-chroot
    creation; follow the MiniOS default for Recommends and Suggests while
    allowing each to be enabled explicitly, and allow refreshing missing APT
    indexes for repository package completion.
  * Make Next Boot management explicit with persistent add controls, clear
    storage-availability diagnostics, reversible module exclusion, and
    confirmed permanent deletion of excluded modules.
  * Delegate Running Now activation and deactivation to MiniOS Tools without
    changing the separately configured Next Boot module set.
  * Support LZ4 consistently across module-creation workflows and explain the
    size/speed trade-offs of available SquashFS compression methods.
  * Improve module inspection with a compact framed file viewer, clipped
    rounded corners, stable search layout, clearer error presentation, and
    authenticated inspection of unreadable active-module backing files when
    required; show cancellable phase progress and streamed diagnostics while
    extracting modules.
  * Improve creation review, progress, and result pages with structured
    summaries, retained phase-aware build logs, human-readable sizes, and
    selectable SHA-256 checksums.
  * Use the canonical application/x-sb MIME type owned by minios-tools instead
    of registering a competing Module Manager MIME definition.
  * Require minios-tools 1.7.0 for reversible Next Boot management, build-base
    selection, LZ4 creation, and the canonical module MIME contract.
  * Require python3-minios-gui 1.4.0 and reuse its help, completion, module
    presentation, operation, chooser, dialog, and structured result widgets.
  * Refresh translations.

 -- crims0n <crims0n@minios.dev>  Mon, 07 Sep 2026 03:09:59 +0300

minios-module-manager (1.0.7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Accept the phase record schema emitted by savechanges
  * Classify savechanges cancellation from its phase and exit status, rejecting
    contradictory terminal records
  * Reject non-object JSON records from all streaming backends
  * Use fixed trusted capture executables and validate the published module,
    result schema, phase sequence, identity, and digest before reporting success

